WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.641
Content Security Policy, usually called
CSP,

2
00:00:02.721 --> 00:00:06.016
is a browser-enforced security policy
delivered by a web application.

3
00:00:06.096 --> 00:00:09.884
The application tells the browser which
resource sources are expected for a page,

4
00:00:09.964 --> 00:00:13.478
and the browser uses that policy when
loading or executing scripts, styles,

5
00:00:13.558 --> 00:00:16.304
images, fonts, frames, connections, and
other resources.

6
00:00:16.384 --> 00:00:19.184
CSP is powerful because enforcement
happens in the browser,

7
00:00:19.264 --> 00:00:22.723
close to the place where many frontend
injection problems become visible.

8
00:00:22.803 --> 00:00:25.000
A CSP does not make insecure code safe by
itself.

9
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:26.672
It is a defense-in-depth control.

10
00:00:26.752 --> 00:00:30.266
Output encoding, safe templates, input
validation, secure framework use,

11
00:00:30.346 --> 00:00:33.805
dependency management, and careful
frontend architecture still matter.

12
00:00:33.885 --> 00:00:37.454
CSP helps reduce the impact of some
injection conditions by limiting what the

13
00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:39.291
browser is allowed to execute or load.

14
00:00:39.371 --> 00:00:41.787
If an attacker-controlled string reaches
the page,

15
00:00:41.867 --> 00:00:45.491
a strong CSP can make successful script
execution harder and easier to detect.

16
00:00:45.571 --> 00:00:49.085
Developers should think of CSP as a
contract between the application and the

17
00:00:49.165 --> 00:00:49.604
browser.

18
00:00:49.684 --> 00:00:51.716
The policy says which scripts are
expected,

19
00:00:51.796 --> 00:00:55.200
which style sources are acceptable, where
images and fonts may come from,

20
00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.629
which APIs the page may connect to, and
which frames or forms are allowed.

21
00:00:58.709 --> 00:01:01.345
A useful policy reflects the application
architecture.

22
00:01:01.425 --> 00:01:03.127
It is specific enough to reduce risk,

23
00:01:03.207 --> 00:01:05.513
flexible enough to support legitimate
behavior,

24
00:01:05.593 --> 00:01:07.460
and maintained as the frontend changes.
